{"model":"llama3.1:8b-instruct-q4_K_M","created_at":"2026-05-26T10:25:41.295588899Z","response":"**Decision: Gestion de Certificados Corporativos en Contenedores Docker**\n===========================================================\n\n### Contexto\n-----------------\n\n* Entorno: WSL2 + Docker, firewall corporativo Fortinet con MITM TLS.\n\n### Sintoma\n--------------\n\nAl intentar realizar `ollama pull`, `npm install` y `pip install` dentro de contenedores se produce el siguiente error:\n```\nx509: certificate signed by unknown authority\n```\n\n### Causa\n---------\n\nLa causa del problema es que el contenedor trae el bundle CA de su imagen base (Debian/Ubuntu/Alpine), sin incluir el CA Fortinet del host.\n\n### Solución\n-------------\n\n#### Fix Debian/Ubuntu\n----------------------\n\n* Montar `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt:/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt:ro` en el contenedor.\n\n#### Fix Alpine\n---------------\n\n* El path destino es `/etc/ssl/cert.pem` (Alpine no utiliza el bundle Debian).\n\n#### Fix Go Binarios\n-------------------\n\n* Pasar `SSL_CERT_FILE=/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt` como variable de entorno.\n\n### Aplicación\n--------------\n\nLa solución se ha aplicado en `~/Workspace/llamalocal/compose/docker-compose.yml` (Ollama, 2026-05-11) y resolvió el problema del pull de modelos.\n\n**Nota:** No aplica a `docker pull \u003cimagen\u003e` ya que el daemon utiliza los CAs del host.\n\n### Anti-patron\n----------------\n\n* Evitar instalar CA dentro de cada Dockerfile (no reproducible entre equipos con CAs distintos).\n\n### Verificación\n-----------------\n\n* Realizar la siguiente prueba: `docker exec \u003ccontainer\u003e curl -fsS https://registry.ollama.ai/` debe devolver un resultado diferente a x509.\n\n## Resumen\n----------\n\nPara resolver el problema de certificados en contenedores Docker, es necesario incluir el CA Fortinet del host en el bundle CA del contenedor. Esto se puede lograr montando `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt:/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt:ro` en el contenedor para Debian/Ubuntu o utilizando `/etc/ssl/cert.pem` para Alpine. Además, es importante evitar instalar CA dentro de cada Dockerfile y utilizar variables de entorno como `SSL_CERT_FILE` para Go binarios que no utilicen SSL_CERT_FILE estandar.","done":true,"done_reason":"stop","context":[128006,882,128007,271,36,417,653,41934,4042,1744,2579,533,64,2246,5928,3429,65566,320,44,74,64207,10441,11,70988,4390,51,57962,1744,2558,58132,653,54526,51594,56511,264,31632,409,1208,14456,409,198,16501,10145,409,671,19256,13,3263,14833,1473,12,469,1257,5808,25,473,16,52163,1624,4733,11,40060,1157,513,55803,473,17,436,5639,4893,320,2014,78,11,41525,11,46774,30540,277,11,29734,27897,4390,12,90082,337,390,264,1189,437,4495,437,320,8729,12,23,11,10566,4733,11412,665,65566,27057,35645,912,665,662,3628,4390,12,97038,83085,6055,409,24723,14452,1533,3001,5296,611,10163,611,11813,8,4502,665,936,5697,627,12,15490,14833,4502,5203,7809,5928,781,281,579,627,12,2360,17459,288,18224,25,4502,653,17889,912,3067,6179,5928,56868,66780,11,76733,653,5456,98519,627,12,13321,1624,54526,25,653,71826,330,567,1838,28999,1,409,220,17,12,18,1584,300,1046,290,4893,382,567,24977,8938,271,75946,25,59471,409,9362,8533,29350,665,687,6901,4692,41649,271,567,13805,10145,271,12,4968,11368,25,468,8143,17,489,41649,11,50977,8533,29350,11246,30976,390,15210,44,42754,627,12,328,396,7942,25,1595,980,3105,6958,7964,47522,4685,379,24547,4685,36228,409,24794,4498,276,390,330,87,12448,25,16125,8667,555,9987,11447,23811,12,356,12119,64,25,658,5593,490,6043,658,13190,9362,409,924,41669,2385,320,1951,13464,14,76752,14,2149,39138,705,7589,658,9362,11246,30976,1624,3552,627,12,16492,468,8143,13835,24215,38401,7208,23066,35014,81691,62134,25409,14,4057,30976,51877,94969,63,46698,2172,379,665,38401,12380,14,25658,2971,15916,81691,62134,25409,94969,19154,12,20295,57707,14,76752,25,6606,38401,12380,14,25658,2971,15916,81691,62134,25409,94969,14712,12380,14,25658,2971,1591